WEBVTT

00:00:03.800 --> 00:00:07.388
Before your live session, there's one step left: the entrance exam.

00:00:07.388 --> 00:00:11.565
You take it in the exam centre on the Gander website, whenever you feel ready.

00:00:12.865 --> 00:00:14.166
Here are the conditions.

00:00:14.166 --> 00:00:18.232
It's twenty multiple-choice questions, picked at random from a larger pool.

00:00:18.232 --> 00:00:19.479
You have sixty minutes.

00:00:19.479 --> 00:00:21.214
The pass mark is eighty percent.

00:00:21.214 --> 00:00:25.388
And it's open book, so keep the S O P and the Knowledge Base open beside you.

00:00:26.688 --> 00:00:28.715
The exam isn't there to catch you out.

00:00:28.715 --> 00:00:32.051
Think of it like a quiz show, where you're answering questions

00:00:32.051 --> 00:00:34.688
to show you understand the North Atlantic region.

00:00:34.688 --> 00:00:38.208
If you've watched these videos and read the S O P, you'll be fine.

00:00:39.508 --> 00:00:41.604
If you don't pass first time, don't worry.

00:00:41.604 --> 00:00:45.248
You can retake after one day, and after seven days for any later attempt.

00:00:45.248 --> 00:00:47.594
Each retake is a fresh random set of questions.

00:00:47.594 --> 00:00:50.489
You only see your result when you finish, not the answers.

00:00:50.489 --> 00:00:52.707
Once you pass, you submit your availability,

00:00:52.707 --> 00:00:55.380
and an instructor picks you up for your live session.

00:00:56.680 --> 00:00:58.237
That's everything you need.

00:00:58.237 --> 00:00:58.813
Good luck.

00:01:00.813 --> 00:01:04.525
And if you ever feel the pressure, picture yourself in the hot seat.

00:01:04.525 --> 00:01:05.672
Here's your question.

00:01:05.672 --> 00:01:07.746
Which ocean does the Nat region cover?

00:01:07.746 --> 00:01:08.347
A, Pacific.

00:01:08.347 --> 00:01:09.002
B, Atlantic.

00:01:09.002 --> 00:01:09.547
C, Indian.

00:01:09.547 --> 00:01:10.093
D, Arctic.

00:01:11.093 --> 00:01:13.193
[Tense music begins, the lights dim]

00:01:13.393 --> 00:01:15.441
Is that your final answer?

00:01:15.793 --> 00:01:20.393
[Tense music builds]

00:01:20.793 --> 00:01:21.593
[Bright chime]

00:01:21.593 --> 00:01:25.412
Correct! It's the Atlantic. Good luck, and we'll see you in your live session.
